      "title": {
        "en": "Dedicated and welcoming grooming personnel"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Pet owners repeatedly praise the styling staff for their warm demeanor, attentive listening, and steady communication prior to appointments. Clients note that groomers discuss specific cut preferences directly and handle anxious or senior dogs with patience and gentle reassurance."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "results",
      "sentiment": "positive",
      "mentions": 16,
      "title": {
        "en": "Attractive styling with occasional complaints"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "The vast majority of reviewers report clean, well-shaped haircuts, especially for doodles and schnauzers, highlighting soft coats and pleasant finishing scents. However, one client expressed frustration over an uneven cut and unexpected delay when grooming two dogs simultaneously."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "animals",
      "sentiment": "positive",
      "mentions": 11,
      "title": {
        "en": "Safe and reassuring pet atmosphere"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Clients appreciate the caring approach taken with rescue pets and elderly dogs that previously experienced grooming stress. Reviewers note that groomers take time to keep animals comfortable throughout baths and hair trims, avoiding the need for veterinary sedation."
      }
    }
  ],
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": {
        "en": "Can senior or grooming-sensitive dogs be accommodated?"
      },
      "a": {
        "en": "Yes, multiple pet parents report that groomers handle elderly and previously reactive dogs with gentle care, eliminating the need for sedation."
      },
